tags: event

= DDP Reformation

Leaders of the German Democratic Party, seeing the party's vote share fall over time, has decided that now is the time to completely reform the party. The party leader, Erich Koch-Weser, has engineered a merger with the political arm of the Young German Order, a nationalist paramilitary group. Now, the party will be called the German State Party, or DStP.

This has led to outcry from the left wing of the party, progressives who would rather not work with antisemites and conservative nationalists.

- @nothing: This is none of our concern.
- @interesting: A merger with a nationalist paramilitary? Is it wrong to see great potential in sanctioning such actions?

@interesting
choose-if: z_party_leader = "Papen"
unavailable-subtitle: On second thought, that's a terrible idea. Why would we ever do it?
subtitle: Franz Von Papen certainly does.
on-arrival: workers_z += 5; unemployed_z +=5; left_dissent += 10; right_strength += 3; right_dissent -= 2; clerical_dissent += 2; dnvp_relations +=5; sh_allied =1;

Franz Von Papen attempts to engineer a merger with the political arm of the nationalist paramilitary group called the Stahlhelm. He had evidently forgotten that said political arm is the DNVP, which is quite a large party itself, and has no need of a merger. However, their leadership is amused at this attempt, and agrees to allow us Stahlhelm protection or our rallies.


@nothing

The DDP's internal affairs are none of our concern.
